# Auto-generated swagger docs are TRACKED, not ignored.
#
# They used to be listed here, which broke two things at once:
#
#  1. internal/api/router.go imports `_ "pad-analyzer/docs"`, so a fresh clone
#     had no docs/docs.go and `go build main.go` / `go vet ./...` failed with
#     "package pad-analyzer/docs is not in std". Only the Docker build worked,
#     because its Dockerfile runs `swag init` before compiling.
#  2. The "OpenAPI Freshness" CI job regenerates them and then asserts
#     `git diff --exit-code docs/`. Against ignored files that diff is always
#     empty, so the job could never fail — and its own error message told you
#     to "commit the result" of a file git was told to ignore.
#
# `swag init -g main.go -o docs --parseDependencyLevel 1` (pinned to the
# go.mod swag version) is byte-reproducible with no embedded timestamps or
# absolute paths, so tracking the output is stable and the drift check is
# meaningful. Regenerate and commit whenever an annotation changes.

